# The HISTORICAL 8-signal-per-period density of flow/tracks/tracks.buda,
# preserved deliberately.
#
# tracks.buda was doubled to 16 signals per period (same rails, same periods,
# same signal metal, half the width and spacing — tools/double_track_density.py).
# That removes so much congestion that some behaviours stop occurring at all:
# flow/hbundles/01_pipeline_hier no longer detours its D0 buses into 3-segment
# Z shapes, so the planner's refinement pass has nothing left to straighten and
# `test_planner_refine` could no longer observe what it exists to guard.
#
# This fixture keeps a CONGESTED input available for tests that need one.  Do
# not "modernize" it — its whole value is being the sparser technology.
def_layer 2 M2 H     55.56
def_layer 3 M3 V     55.56
def_layer 4 M4 H     55.56
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 50
def_layer 6 M6 H TOP 52.94
def_layer 7 M7 V TOP 56.10

# Track patterns are REQUIRED for Detailed NUTS
# Format: <layer_id> <origin> [<type> <width> <spacing>] ...
def_track_pattern 2 -100  POWER 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  GROUND 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5
def_track_pattern 3    0  POWER 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  GROUND 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5
def_track_pattern 4 -200  POWER 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  GROUND 2 1  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5  SIGNAL 1 0.5
def_track_pattern 5    0  POWER 3 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  GROUND 3 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1
def_track_pattern 6 -400  POWER 4 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  GROUND 4 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1
def_track_pattern 7 -600  POWER 6 2  SIGNAL 3 2  SIGNAL 3 2  SIGNAL 3 2  GROUND 2 1  SIGNAL 3 2  SIGNAL 3 2  SIGNAL 3 2

report_overhead
